</pre></div><h2 class="h2">Conclusion</h2><p>The incorporated image caption generator is efficient as far as it integrates InceptionV3, which performs the extraction of image features, with LSTM, which generates the captions across times. To train the model, the Flickr8K dataset was used, where the captions have been tokenized and cleaned. Captions were generated under both greedy and beam search, and beam search was a little better in terms of BLEU scores.</p><p>The model had a great performance in generating coherent human-like captions. Visualization also verified that the model was accurate in capturing the context of images. On the whole, the system managed to connect natural language processing with computer vision.</p><hr/><div class="nexttopicdiv"><span class="nexttopictext">Next Topic</span><span class="nexttopiclink"><a href="dog-breed-classification-using-transfer-learning">Dog Breed Classification using Transfer Learning</a></span></div><br/> <div id="bottomnext"><a class="next" href="resnet-residual-network" style="float:left">← prev</a> <a class="next" href="dog-breed-classification-using-transfer-learning" style="float:right">next →</a></div><br/> </td></tr></tbody></table></div></body></html><br/></div><div class="related-posts-container"><h2 class="h3">Related Posts</h2><ul class="related-posts-list"><li><a class="related-post-item" href="word-embedding-in-natural-language-processing"><h3 class="h3">Word Embedding in Natural Language Processing</h3><p class="related-post-content">Word embeddings are a set of numerical vectors with reduced dimensions providing information of a semantic and syntactic nature for the corresponding words. They are very crucial in Natural Language Processing tasks. In this article, both classical and neural methods such as TF-IDF, Word2Vec and...</p><p class="reading-time"><i aria-hidden="true" class="fa fa-clock-o"></i> 16 min read <span class="arrow-position"><svg fill="currentColor" height="1.3rem" stroke="currentColor